{"type":"message","id":"0d964a2c","parentId":"59cf77cf","timestamp":"2026-04-15T00:51:43.421Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_gvqd2063znkr_3","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"openclaw browser configuration chrome executable path headless\",\n  \"provider\": \"miaoda\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"浏览器(OpenClaw 托管) | Docs | OpenClaw\",\n      \"url\": \"https://openclaws.io/zh/docs/tools/browser\",\n      \"description\": \"headless: false,\\nnoSandbox: false,\\nattachOnly: false,\\nexecutablePath: \\\"/Applications/Brave Browser.app/Contents/MacOS/Brave Browser\\\",\\n设置 <代码开始>browser.executablePath<代码结束> 可以覆盖自动检测：\\nCLI 示例：\\n<代码开始>openclaw config set browser.executablePath \\\"/usr/bin/google-chrome\\\"<代码结束>\\n<代码开始>\\n// macOS\\n{\\nbrowser:...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"config - OpenClaw\",\n      \"url\": \"https://openclaw-docs.beaverslab.xyz/en/cli/config\",\n      \"description\": \"On this page\\nopenclaw config\\nExamples\\nPaths\\nValues\\nSubcommands\\nValidate\\nCLI commands\\nconfig\\n<beginning of the code>openclaw config<end of the code>\\nConfig helpers: get/set/unset/validate values by path and print the active config file. Run without a subcommand to open the configure wizard (same as <beginning of the code>openclaw configure<end of the code>).\\nExamples\\nopencl...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"openclaw/docs/tools/browser.md at main · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/main/docs/tools/browser.md\",\n      \"description\": \"749 lines (581 loc) · 28.5 KB\\n<table>\\n<tr><th>summary</th><th>read_when</th><th>title</th></tr>\\n<tr><td>Integrated browser control service + action commands</td><td>Adding agent-controlled browser automation\\nDebugging why openclaw is interfering with your own Chrome\\nImplementing browser settings + lifecycle in the macOS app</td><td>Browser (Open...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Browser Automation\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.openclawdoc.com/docs/agents/browser-automation/\",\n      \"description\": \"Browser Automation\\nOpenClaw's agent-browser module gives agents the ability to control a real web browser. Agents can navigate websites, fill out forms, click buttons, take screenshots, and extract structured data from web pages -- all programmatically.\\nPrerequisites\\nBefore using browser automation, install the browser engine:\\nopenclaw browser install\\nThis downloads a compatible Chromium binary. You can also point OpenClaw to an existing Chrome installation:\\nbrowser:\\n  executable: /usr...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Browser Troubleshooting\",\n      \"url\": \"https://docs.openclaw.ai/tools/browser-linux-troubleshooting\",\n      \"description\": \"On this page\\nBrowser Troubleshooting (Linux)\\nProblem: “Failed to start Chrome CDP on port 18800”\\nRoot Cause\\nSolution 1: Install Google Chrome (Recommended)\\nSolution 2: Use Snap Chromium with Attach-Only Mode\\nVerifying the Browser Works\\nConfig Reference\\nProblem: “No Chrome tabs found for profile=“user\\\"\\\"\\nBrowser\\nBrowser Troubleshooting\\nBrowser Troubleshooting (Linux)\\nProblem: “...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"OpenClaw Browser 工具完全指南\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/geekjourneyx/awesome-openclaw/blob/main/docs/browser-guide-zh.md\",\n      \"description\": \"934 lines (705 loc) · 19.3 KB\\nOpenClaw Browser 工具完全指南\\n目录\\n概述\\n工作原理\\n浏览器模式对比\\nUbuntu/Linux 安装\\n配置说明\\n配置文件详解\\nCLI 命令参考\\nSnapshot 与 Refs\\n高级功能\\n远程浏览器\\nChrome 扩展模式\\n安全最佳实践\\n故障排查\\n概述\\nOpenClaw Browser 工具允许 AI Agent 控制一个专用的浏览器实例，实现：...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"[Bug]: Browser Service fails to start Chrome CDP in Docker container - WebSocket timeout on port 18791 #16644\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/16644\",\n      \"description\": \"Configure browser service in...\\nRenamed browser profile from \\\"openclaw\\\" → \\\"chrome\\\" so the agent's browser tool finds and uses the managed Chromium instead of the extension relay\\nSet defaultProfile: \\\"chrome\\\"\\nSet enabled: true, attachOnly: false\\nSet executablePath: \\\"/usr/bin/chromium\\\"\\nDefined cdpPort: 18800 explicitly in the profile\\nSynchronized all token references (gateway.auth.token, gateway.remote.token, hooks.\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Browser (OpenClaw-managed)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://molty.finna.ai/docs/tools/browser\",\n      \"description\": \"Browser (OpenClaw-managed)\\nOpenClaw can run a dedicated Chrome/Brave/Edge/Chromium profile that the agent controls. It is isolated from your personal browser and is managed through a small local control service inside the Gateway (loopback only).\\nBeginner view:\\nThink of it as a separate, agent-only browser.\\nThe <beginning of the code>openclaw<end of the code> profile does not touch your personal browser profile.\\nThe...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"openclaw/docs/tools/browser.md at 8f58982830d3b95430b70f5fc4d1e8a82a99fd4a · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/8f58982830d3b95430b70f5fc4d1e8a82a99fd4a/docs/tools/browser.md\",\n      \"description\": \"ShawnPana\\n709 lines (552 loc) · 27.4 KB\\n<table>\\n<tr><th>summary</th><th>read_when</th><th>title</th></tr>\\n<tr><td>Integrated browser control service + action commands</td><td>Adding agent-controlled browser automation\\nDebugging why openclaw is interfering with your own Chrome\\nImplementing browser settings + lifecycle in the macOS app</td><...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Browser Troubleshooting (Linux)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://openclawlab.com/docs/tools/browser-linux-troubleshooting/\",\n      \"description\": \"Problem: “Failed to start Chrome CDP on port 18800”\\nMoltbot...\\nOn Ubuntu (and many Linux distros), the default Chromium installation is a snap package. Snap’s AppArmor confinement interferes with how Moltbot spawns and monitors the browser process.\\nThe <beginning of the code>apt install chromium<end of the code> command installs a stub package that redirects to snap:\\n<beginning of the code>\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"openclaw browser configuration chrome executable path headless","provider":"miaoda","count":10,"results":[{"title":"浏览器(OpenClaw 托管) | Docs | OpenClaw","url":"https://openclaws.io/zh/docs/tools/browser","description":"headless: false,\nnoSandbox: false,\nattachOnly: false,\nexecutablePath: \"/Applications/Brave Browser.app/Contents/MacOS/Brave Browser\",\n设置 <代码开始>browser.executablePath<代码结束> 可以覆盖自动检测：\nCLI 示例：\n<代码开始>openclaw config set browser.executablePath \"/usr/bin/google-chrome\"<代码结束>\n<代码开始>\n// macOS\n{\nbrowser:...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"config - OpenClaw","url":"https://openclaw-docs.beaverslab.xyz/en/cli/config","description":"On this page\nopenclaw config\nExamples\nPaths\nValues\nSubcommands\nValidate\nCLI commands\nconfig\n<beginning of the code>openclaw config<end of the code>\nConfig helpers: get/set/unset/validate values by path and print the active config file. Run without a subcommand to open the configure wizard (same as <beginning of the code>openclaw configure<end of the code>).\nExamples\nopencl...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"openclaw/docs/tools/browser.md at main · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/main/docs/tools/browser.md","description":"749 lines (581 loc) · 28.5 KB\n<table>\n<tr><th>summary</th><th>read_when</th><th>title</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Integrated browser control service + action commands</td><td>Adding agent-controlled